      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-03-20T19:26:56Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "what about undoing the settings on error... or perhaps better, don\u0027t set the new values until after verifying?",
      "revId": "6600ba5dca3990e48f2322fdda09058455509989",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "02f34f0f_12f46c9a",
        "filename": "drivers/android/binder.c",
        "patchSetId": 4
      },
      "lineNbr": 917,
      "author": {
        "id": 1869395
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-03-20T23:13:08Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Changing the settings will have an impact on transactions PI. These values are still used to determine the minimum node priority. So I don\u0027t know that clearing them will have a positive performance impact.\n\nThe idea here is to flag userspace misconfiguration. This change doesn\u0027t really target a \"problem\" with the driver\u0027s behavior.\n\nI could explore the idea of clearing these values which is basically the same as forcing: SCHED_NORMAL, nice(0) and !inherit_rt. However, this would require doing a deeper performance testing.",
      "parentUuid": "bbd95ea9_e5ec82e8",
      "revId": "6600ba5dca3990e48f2322fdda09058455509989",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "55c54b7b_1dce2412",
        "filename": "drivers/android/binder.c",
        "patchSetId": 4
      },
      "lineNbr": 917,
      "author": {
        "id": 1069543
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-03-20T23:28:02Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Oh, I thought the `!capable(CAP_SYS_NICE) \u0026\u0026 !rlimit(...)` meant that it is not allowed to promote. We\u0027re just promoting anyway?",
      "parentUuid": "02f34f0f_12f46c9a",
      "revId": "6600ba5dca3990e48f2322fdda09058455509989",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "3a9df35b_f672bc5f",
        "filename": "drivers/android/binder.c",
        "patchSetId": 4
      },
      "lineNbr": 917,
      "author": {
        "id": 1869395
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-03-20T23:33:15Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "It won\u0027t be allowed to be promoted to X. However, X is still determined by these \"minimum node priority\" settings. If we change the settings then X can become a different value (lower), and the kernel could allow a downgrade.\n\nI don\u0027t think we want to lower the \"minimum node priority\" just because a process can\u0027t inherit realtime.",
      "parentUuid": "55c54b7b_1dce2412",
      "revId": "6600ba5dca3990e48f2322fdda09058455509989",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "f7452a31_814a8c69",
        "filename": "drivers/android/binder.c",
        "patchSetId": 4
      },
      "lineNbr": 917,
      "author": {
        "id": 1069543
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-03-20T23:58:25Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Ok. Staying compatible is the right thing for now. Are you planning to follow up on all the offenders who come up? I suspect this new message will cause quite a few bugs to come your way (even though it is someone else\u0027s issue).\n\nSince it is only in android-mainline, not many folks will notice it (for now). Are you planning to backport this to GKI kernels?",
      "parentUuid": "3a9df35b_f672bc5f",
      "revId": "6600ba5dca3990e48f2322fdda09058455509989",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "fdef00b0_e8073553",
        "filename": "drivers/android/binder.c",
        "patchSetId": 4
      },
      "lineNbr": 917,
      "author": {
        "id": 1869395
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-03-21T00:15:04Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Yes, I was planning on following up on all offenders. However, let me confirm with smoreland@ that this is actually an error on HIDL, as we are setting `inherit_rt` unconditionally there.",
      "parentUuid": "f7452a31_814a8c69",
      "revId": "6600ba5dca3990e48f2322fdda09058455509989",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    }
